---
description: One ActiveRecord table per migration file
globs: db/migrate/**/*.rb
alwaysApply: false
---

# One table per migration

Do not create multiple tables in a single migration.

```ruby
# BAD
class CreateOpsDesk < ActiveRecord::Migration[8.1]
  def change
    create_table :organizations do |t|
      t.string :name, null: false
      t.timestamps
    end
    create_table :customers do |t|
      t.references :organization, null: false, foreign_key: true
      t.timestamps
    end
  end
end

# GOOD
class CreateOrganizations < ActiveRecord::Migration[8.1]
  def change
    create_table :organizations do |t|
      t.string :name, null: false
      t.timestamps
    end
  end
end
```

Adding columns or foreign keys to an existing table is its own migration. That file must not call `create_table`.
